From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: meta-rzg3l-fast-anime-logo <fastboot@example.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] video: rzg2l: select the 1080p display mode

The driver defaults to MIPI_DSI_720P.  This layer's boot animation is
1920x1080, so the bootloader has to bring the pipeline up at 1080p or the
hand-over cannot be seamless: the kernel pins the HDMI connector to the
single CEA VIC the bootloader programmed, and the player then looks for a
mode matching its artwork.  At 720p the player would find no usable mode
and skip the animation, leaving the static splash on screen until weston.

DISPLAY_MODE also selects which file rzg2l_video_init() loads, so this one
line moves the load to boot/boot_img_1080p.bin.gz, which is where
rzg3l-anime-logo-assets installs the animation's first frame.

1920x1080@60 is exactly the ADV7535's ceiling and passes both of the
driver's limits rather than exceeding them: adv7533_mode_valid() checks
mode->clock against max_mode_clock_khz (148500 == 148500) and
mode->clock * 24 against max_lane_freq_khz * 4 (3564000 == 3564000).

define_1080p.h carries 2200x1125 total at 148.5 MHz with positive syncs,
which is CEA VIC 16 value for value, so the mode the kernel advertises and
the mode the hardware is scanning out are the same mode.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [RZ/G3L boot animation, board specific]
---
 drivers/video/rzg2l/rzg2l_video.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/video/rzg2l/rzg2l_video.c
+++ b/drivers/video/rzg2l/rzg2l_video.c
@@ -32,7 +32,15 @@
 #define	LVDS_720P		2
 #define PARALLEL_RGB_720P	3

-#define	DISPLAY_MODE MIPI_DSI_720P
+/*
+ * 1080p, to match the 1920x1080 boot animation this layer ships and the
+ * CEA VIC 16 the kernel pins the connector to.  These three have to agree:
+ * U-Boot programs the hardware from define_1080p.h, the kernel advertises
+ * exactly one mode and refuses everything else, and the player selects the
+ * mode that matches its artwork.  Changing one without the other two gets
+ * you a connector pinned to a mode the hardware is not scanning out.
+ */
+#define	DISPLAY_MODE MIPI_DSI_1080P

 #if (DISPLAY_MODE == MIPI_DSI_1080P)
 #include "define_1080p.h"
